12:21:38.425 world 0 channel 0 listening on 127.0.0.1:8485
12:21:38.426 database C:\MapleCW\maplecw.db
12:21:38.426 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
12:21:38.426   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
12:21:38.426 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
12:21:38.426   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
12:21:38.426   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
12:21:38.426   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
12:21:38.426   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
12:21:38.426   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
12:21:38.426   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
12:21:38.426   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
12:21:38.426   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
12:21:38.426   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
12:21:38.426   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
12:21:38.426   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
12:21:38.426   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
